  "lineage": "Brega and tecnobrega Brazilian popular-music genres of the northern Brazilian Amazonian Pará state (especially Belém). Brega (\"kitsch\") originated as a mid-late-twentieth-century commercial sentimental-popular music; tecnobrega is its 2000s-onward electronic-DIY remix-and-production reformulation, with characteristic synthesizer-and-808-drum-machine production, fast tempo, and an outdoor-aparelhagem sound-system street-party performance context. Distinguished from sertanejo by brega's northern-Amazonian-Brazilian regional base.",
